WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.180
As more Conjuring movies are added to the
franchise, keeping track of things can get

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.180
confusing, especially since they jump around
chronologically.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.160
Luckily, we’ve figured out when everything
takes place.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.340
From freaky nuns to haunted houses, here's
the entire Conjuring Universe story explained.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.660
Chronologically speaking, The Conjuring Universe
all starts with The Nun.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:28.540
The film takes place in 1952, at the Abbey
of St. Carta in Romania, where Father Burke

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:34.140
and a novitiate, Sister Irene, are investigating
the death of one of the abbey's nuns.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.399
They discover the nuns have been spending
most of their time praying in shifts to keep

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:43.269
a nun-shaped evil entity from hitchhiking
its way out into the real world on a human

00:00:43.269 --> 00:00:43.760
host.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.700
As it turns out, the abbey was originally
built by a duke during the Middle Ages who

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.780
was more interested in demon worship than
Catholicism.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.880
He managed to raise the demon Valak but was
stopped by a group of Christian knights who

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.140
were able to seal Valak for a while.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:04.300
With the help of a local man named Frenchie,
Father Burke and Sister Irene seem to finally

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.160
banish Valak back to Hell.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:12.060
But as it happens, Valak manages to hitch
a supernatural ride out of town on Frenchie's

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:12.560
back.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:19.020
The story of Annabelle starts in 1943 with
Annabelle: Creation, when a dollmaker named

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:24.360
Samuel Mullins and his wife Esther lose their
seven-year-old daughter, Annabelle, in a freak

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.240
car accident.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.320
About 12 years later, the Mullins open their
doors to a group of orphaned girls and the

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.180
nun tasked with their care.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.800
When one of the orphans stumbles upon a porcelain
doll in a locked bedroom, she unwittingly

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.140
releases a demon that wreaks havoc on the
house and its inhabitants.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.480
It's soon revealed that the Mullins had been
tricked into letting a demon take possession

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.900
of one of Samuel's dolls, and it's now decided
to try and find a human host.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:55.960
By the end of the ordeal, the demon has succeeded
in possessing the unlucky orphan, who escapes

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:01.400
and, now going by the name Annabelle, winds
up being adopted by a nice family in Santa

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:01.900
Monica.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:08.580
There, she grows up, runs away, joins a cult,
and then returns to murder her adoptive parents.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.640
As it turns out, the poor adopted parents
of Annabelle live next door to John and Mia

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.360
Form, the main protagonists of 2014's Annabelle.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:23.980
John has given his wife Mia an antique porcelain
doll as a gift for their unborn child.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.300
But after Annabelle and her boyfriend kill
her parents, they move on to the Form residence,

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.440
where Annabelle immediately takes a liking
to Mia's antique doll.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.120
"I like your dolls."

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.740
When the human Annabelle dies, the demon hops
into the doll.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.780
Terror sets in as the newly demonic doll decides
to torment the Form family.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.310
Willing to trade her own soul to save her
newborn daughter, Mia tries to jump out of

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.019
her window with the doll.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:03:00.290
Luckily, John and Mia's friend Evelyn arrive
in time to stop her, and Evelyn sacrifices

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.000
herself to save the family.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.730
In the end, an unsuspecting woman buys the
doll from a toyshop as a gift for her daughter,

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:08.720
a nurse.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:14.540
In The Conjuring, we revisit that nurse who
is now at the mercy of the demon spirit trapped

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.560
inside the toy.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.560
So the Warrens take the doll off the nurse's
hands and move on to their next case.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:27.040
In 1971, the Warrens are teaching a class
on demonology at Massachusetts Western University.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:32.340
During the lecture, they play footage of a
possessed man named Maurice, who Ed explains

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.140
killed himself after attempting to shoot his
wife.

00:03:35.469 --> 00:03:40.879
Maurice is Frenchie, the nice guy who spent
some time in Romania in the '50s and came

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.140
home with a demon nun as a souvenir.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:49.700
One of the attendees at the Warrens' demonology
lecture is Carolyn Perron, whose family has

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.280
recently moved into a Rhode Island farmhouse.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.440
Unfortunately, they're now being tormented
by a malevolent, clap-happy spirit.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.279
After some digging, the Warrens discover the
house was built on land that once belonged

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.779
to a witch named Bathsheba.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.580
Unfortunately, that discovery comes a little
late.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:13.079
Bathsheba has already set her sights on Carolyn,
and the now-possessed mother brings her kids

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.620
back to the house to kill them.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:20.470
The Warrens show up just in time, and the
curse of Bathsheba is lifted, finally leaving

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.680
the Perrons with a livable farmhouse.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.840
When Ed and Lorraine Warren are needed on
an overnight investigation, they hire a girl

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:33.080
named Mary Ellen to stay over and keep an
eye on their daughter, Judy.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:37.980
Unfortunately, Mary Ellen's friend Daniela
drops by the house uninvited.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:44.259
She finds a way into the Warrens' artifact
room, disturbs Annabelle, and unleashes every

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.340
ghost and demon the Warrens have trapped in
their basement.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:52.600
The girls spend the night essentially playing
hide and seek with a bunch of possessed objects

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:56.120
before Annabelle is returned to her case once
and for all.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:03.160
In 1973, Anna Tate-Garcia is a social worker
who gets mixed up with La Llorona when she

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:09.020
takes the sons of a woman named Patricia Alvarez
to the police, unwittingly allowing the titular

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.760
spirit access to kill them.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:16.740
As a result, Anna's own children are targeted
by the spirit, so Anna seeks help from Father

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:21.440
Perez, the priest from Annabelle who obviously
has some experience with evil beings.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.660
He tells her about a former priest named Rafael
Olvera who can banish the entity.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:31.400
One banished spirit later, and Anna and her
children are safe, although she keeps the

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:33.880
necklace that once belonged to the wailing
woman.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.120
In a deleted scene, it's revealed that she
hands the necklace over to Rafael.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.100
"What are you going to do with this?"

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.160
"I know a couple on the east coast who look
after things like this."

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:50.640
Valak makes its return in 1976 during The
Conjuring 2, the film that sees Ed and Lorraine

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.360
Warren seemingly defeat the spirit for good.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:59.920
Beginning in 1976, the Warrens are investigating
the infamous Amityville murders, and Lorraine

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:04.760
has a vision where she comes face to face
with Valak and a vision of her husband's death.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:10.879
Lorraine continues to see visions of the demon
nun, even as the pair travel to Enfield, England,

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.480
where the Hodgson family has been experiencing
paranormal activity.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:20.240
When it appears as though the entire haunting
is a hoax put on by the family to gain fame,

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.280
the Warrens pack up their things to leave.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:27.410
But Lorraine soon realizes that Valak has
been behind the entire thing, and they return

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.180
to the house in a last ditch effort to save
the family.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:36.060
Ed almost falls to his death in the process,
leaving Lorraine to go head to head with Valak

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:36.560
herself.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.960
She succeeds in banishing the demon by using
its name and pulls Ed to safety.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.040
"You are Valak.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.420
The Defiler.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.600
The profane.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.660
The marquis of snakes."

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:55.600
The day is saved, and everything seems to
be going smoothly...at least until the next

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.340
film in the franchise gets released.

